  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   The Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem seeks to find a function h : [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] with integral 1 that minimizes the maximum overlap integral against its shifted versions. We are given an initial solution with n_points=95, C5\u22480.3808. The goal is to find a better solution (C5<0.3808) by:\n   - Using a constructive optimization method on the initial grid (95 points)\n   - Projecting solutions to finer grids (199 points) for potentially better resolution\n   - Implementing a local search optimization with gradient information where feasible\n   - Balancing between search on current grid and projection to finer grids\n   - Ensuring feasibility (0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and \u2211h[i]=n/2) through projection and normalization\n   The bottleneck is computational time for fine grids, so we alternate between local optimization and grid projection.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n   Given a grid size n_points, define:\n     - dx = 2/n_points (spatial step)\n     - Objective function: minimize C5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx, approximated by:\n           dx * max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full'))\n     - Constraint: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 for all i, and \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n     - For grid projection between n_old and n_new:\n         h_new[i] = h_old[round((i * (n_points-1)) / (n_old-1))]\n         Normalize to satisfy \u2211h_new[i] = n_points/2 by scaling\n         Clip values to [0,1] to maintain feasibility\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - validate_parent(n_points): Ensure initial solution has correct sum and normalized to [0,1]\n   - optimize_local(grid_values, n_points, time_limit=600):\n        Use local search with gradient descent and constraints projection\n        Implement box and integral constraint handling\n        Custom gradient calculation for overlap integral\n   - run_initial_grid(budget):\n        Start at given parent grid (95 points), use local search to improve\n        Track best solution and intermediate projections\n   - run_fine_grid(parent_h, budget, coarse_grid_size=95):\n        Project parent_h to 199-point grid\n        Apply local search with strict feasibility constraints\n   - Main loop:\n        First optimize on 95-point grid\n        If time allows, optimize on 199-point grid\n        Output best solution found\n\n4. Search Choices:\n   - Primary method: Local search with projected gradient\n   - Secondary grid: 199 points for finer resolution\n   - Projection method: Round interpolation then normalize\n   - Local search parameters:\n        Gradient step: 1e-2\n        Temperature schedule: Linear decrease from 0.1 to 0.001 over optimization\n        Constraint handling: \n            Integral constraint: Scale entire vector \n            Box constraints: Clip to [0,1]\n   - Multiple restarts: 5 restarts per grid if time allows\n   - Cooling schedule: 5000 steps, adaptive step size\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\n   - Primary grid (95 points): ~800s for local search\n   - Secondary grid (199 points): Dedicated ~500s after primary completes\n   - Feasibility check: Automatically handle with projection and normalization\n   - Fallback: Return best candidate from complete run if optimization fails\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n   - Check candidate: Ensure 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and \u2211h[i]\u2248n/2, finite overlap values\n   - Returned values: h_values (sampled at 95/199 points), improved C5, grid size\n   - Output format: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n   - Constraint handling: Enforced through projection and gradient damping",
